; Exits that flood (read by src/weather.c at boot).
;
; One exit per line: <room vnum> <direction>.  The exit back the other way
; floods too, if there is one.  Lines starting with ';' are comments, and
; the file ends with '$'.
;
; A zone's rivers rise during spring rain (+1 an hour for rain, +2 for a
; downpour, +3 for a thunderstorm or tornado, -1 for any other spring
; weather, -2 an hour outside spring).  At level 6 of 12 the zone floods
; and these exits close to everyone but immortals until the level falls
; back to 2.  Players in the rooms are told when the water rises and falls,
; 'weather' says when the local rivers are in flood, and NPC routines walk
; around flooded exits.

